**Files created (nothing else touched, no commit):**
- `src/mem_mcp/util_text.py`: `slugify_title(title: str) -> str`.
  - It lowercases and strips the input, then replaces runs of `[^a-z0-9]+` with `-` using the module-level `_NON_ALNUM_RE`, then strips hyphens at both ends.
  - It has `from __future__ import annotations`, a module docstring explaining the ASCII-only choice, and a short function docstring.
- `tests/unit/test_util_text.py`: DB-free parametrized sync tests covering:
  - normal text and whitespace;
  - punctuation collapsing and edge stripping;
  - digits;
  - empty, whitespace-only and punctuation-only input;
  - unicode: `"Café"` → `"caf"`, `"Café Déjà Vu"` → `"caf-d-j-vu"`, `"Ünïcödé Title"` → `"n-c-d-title"`, `"日本語"` → `""`;
  - no `--` and no leading or trailing `-` in the result.

